    "body": "I agree with Ian's historical argument that \"positive\", by itself, is genuinely unclear whether zero is included or not. Whether zero is positive, negative, or neither varies by context (in the real numbers it's neither, in JS it's either positive *or* negative, etc), so one *cannot* infer generally that \"positive\" includes or excludes zero.\r\n\r\nHowever, I agree that the wording currently used is awkward. I recommend \"positive non-zero number\", as a shorter and either equally or *more* clear wording.",
